# Windows launchers MUST be checked out with CRLF line endings.
#
# cmd.exe parses a .bat by byte offset rather than by line: given a file whose
# lines end in a bare LF it seeks to the wrong position and starts executing
# mid-line, producing storms of
#   "'...' is not recognized as an internal or external command"
# Windows Script Host is more forgiving, but CRLF is still the correct form.
#
# Without these rules the line endings depend on the *cloner's* core.autocrlf:
# Git for Windows defaults to true (checks out CRLF, so everything looks fine),
# but core.autocrlf=false / input — or cloning on a non-Windows host and running
# the scripts over a share — yields LF and breaks 启动服务.bat /
# 重启服务(管理员).bat. `text` keeps LF in the repository and `eol=crlf` forces
# CRLF in every working tree, so the scripts work for everyone.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
